> Original ten-slot even-id live chain

Retain ten old slots, root0 and chain0-to2-to4-to6-to8, with all odd ids
unreachable. The actual survivor order is[0,2,4,6,8], with new slots[0,1,2,3,4].
The original-id forwarding table contains minus one for every unreachable slot.
The new survivor-field rows form0-to1-to2-to3-to4, and the actual root becomes
slot0.

The figure compares old survivor slots with actual dense new slots against the
identity reference. Both axes use identical numerical and physical scales.
Stable order means old ids remain increasing in the new slot order; it does not
preserve each original address. Denseness means no holes in this abstract
unit-slot result, not a statement that arbitrary-sized C++ objects have been
physically relocated in memory.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/mark_compact_original.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto a =
        dm::algorithms::mark_compact_analyze(dm::algorithms::mark_compact_demo_graph());
    std::vector<double> x, y;
    std::print("| actual original slot | actual final live mark | actual new slot or minus1 |\n| ---: | " "---: | ---: |\n");
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < a.result.marked.size(); ++i) {
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} |\n", i, int(a.result.marked[i]),
                   a.result.new_address[i]);
        if (a.result.marked[i]) {
            x.push_back(i);
            y.push_back(a.result.new_address[i]);
        }
    }
    std::print("\n| actual new owner slot | actual field index | actual translated target slot |\n| ---: | " "---: | ---: |\n");
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < a.result.updated_refs.size(); ++i)
        for (std::size_t j = 0; j < a.result.updated_refs[i].size(); ++j)
            std::print("| {} | {} | {} |\n", i, j, a.result.updated_refs[i][j]);
    std::print("\nActual live output slots {}; actual relocated first root {}.\n",
               a.result.order.size(), a.relocated_roots.front());
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    p.line({0, 9}, {0, 9}, "identity reference", {148, 163, 184}, 1).points(
        x, y, "actual survivors", {37, 99, 235}, 6).size(850, 850).margins(
        95, 35, 60, 70).x_limits(-.5, 9.5).y_limits(-.5, 9.5).title(
        "Original even-id chain: actual stable dense slot map").x_label(
        "original live object slot").y_label("actual new compacted slot").save_svg("build/mark_compact_original.svg");
}
```
