> Alias, cycle and root preservation

A single completed map must be used everywhere. If two fields reference the same
old object, both become the same new slot. Field order and duplicate targets are
retained. Cyclic references remain cyclic after translation. Original root order
and duplicate roots are retained in the new analysis API’s relocated_roots
vector; the historical MarkCompactResult keeps its original field layout and
callers needing roots should use the analysis result.

The next exact graph has duplicate fields0-to2, a live2-to4-to2 cycle, and
original roots[0,0,4]. Its surviving old ids are[0,2,4], translated fields
are[[1,1],[2],[1]], and roots become[0,0,2]. Old3-to5 is unreachable and
omitted. The table preserves every actual field/root slot even where graph
geometry shares the same drawn edge. The figure annotates the actual two aliases
from new0 to new1 rather than suggesting distinct target objects.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/mark_compact_aliases.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    dm::algorithms::ObjectGraph g{6, {{2, 2}, {}, {4}, {5}, {2}, {}}, {0, 0, 4},
                                  {}};
    auto t = dm::algorithms::mark_compact_trace(g);
    auto &a = t.analysis;
    std::print("| actual old owner | actual new owner | actual original field slot | actual old target | " "actual new target |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (auto &r : t.references)
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", r.owner_old, r.owner_new,
                   r.field, r.target_old, r.target_new);
    std::print("\n| actual original root slot | actual old root | actual relocated root |\n| ---: | ---: | " "---: |\n");
    for (auto &r : t.roots)
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} |\n", r.slot, r.old_id, r.new_slot);
    dm::graphics::Diagram d;
    d.node("0", {0, 0},
           std::format("Actual new slot0\nold object{}", a.result.order[0])).node("1", {6, 3}, std::format("Actual new slot1\nold object{}", a.result.order[1])).node("2", {6, -3}, std::format("Actual new slot2\nold object{}", a.result.order[2])).edge("0", "1", std::format("{} actual alias fields", a.result.updated_refs[0].size())).edge("1", "2").edge("2", "1");
    d.save_svg("build/mark_compact_aliases.svg");
}
