> Actual phases and the limits of the slot model

The shared canonical liveness producer validates the complete graph before
indexing, including unreachable bad fields, then marks on pushing. Roots and
fields are examined in their original order, with pending objects popped LIFO;
duplicate roots/fields and cycles never cause duplicate pushes. The trace owns
that one real marking history plus every actual old-slot forwarding decision and
each live-field/root rewrite. It never reruns reachability or infers phase
histories from the final map.

Total complete validation, traversal and rewriting work is O(N+E+R). This
implementation owns marks, a stack, a forwarding vector, survivor order,
translated fields and relocated roots, requiring O(N+E_live+R) result/working
storage in addition to input. It computes graph/layout metadata; it neither
moves/frees C++ payloads nor rewrites raw pointers, and it is not an in-place
physical collector. The earlier no-extra-space description concerned a different
implementation model and does not describe these returned C++ containers.

Every object occupies one modeled slot. ObjectGraph.sizes metadata is entirely
ignored by these slot collectors, even if supplied values would be invalid for a
size-aware method. The independent control below supplies size100 for every
original object and verifies that the actual forwarding map remains unchanged.
No byte-address claim is inferred from those ignored values. Empty roots leave
every object unreachable; an empty valid graph yields an empty result.

Actual capture admission includes marking’s2*N+E+R+S base input/mark slots and
its real root/pop/live-field events, plus each actual forward/live-field/root
record. Default cap is one million; zero disables the optional cap. Fields
within records, row headers, capacities, returned/runtime mark/result copies and
physical bytes are excluded. Captures own the original graph once and are
complete or throw. No external dataset is needed for these exact graph/layout
controls.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/mark_compact_work.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto g = dm::algorithms::mark_compact_demo_graph();
    auto a = dm::algorithms::mark_compact_analyze(g);
    g.sizes.assign(g.num_objects, 100);
    auto b = dm::algorithms::mark_compact_analyze(g);
    auto &w = a.work;
    std::print("Actual forwarding unchanged under supplied size100 metadata: {}.\n\n| actual phase " "observation | actual count |\n| --- | ---: |\n| initialized mark slots | {} |\n| complete " "validated fields including garbage | {} |\n| actual live-object pops | {} |\n| actual " "forwarding slots | {} |\n| actual translated live fields | {} |\n| actual translated root " "slots | {} |\n",
               a.result.new_address == b.result.new_address,
               w.marking.initialized, w.marking.validation.references,
               w.marking.pops, w.scanned, w.rewritten, w.roots);
    auto p =
        dm::graphics::RPlot::barplot({double(w.marking.initialized),
                                      double(w.marking.validation.references),
                                      double(w.marking.pops), double(w.scanned),
                                      double(w.rewritten), double(w.roots)},
                                     {"mark slots", "guard fields", "live pops",
                                      "forward scan", "new fields", "root slots"},
                                     "actual operations", {37, 99, 235});
    p.x_label("producing phase or guard").y_label("actual selected operation count");
    p.title("Original graph: actual unit-slot collection phases").save_svg(
        "build/mark_compact_work.svg");
}
```
